{"id":"n-20261010-i34slf","category":"travel","display_title":"Hitchhiking Across Australia","display_title_he":"טרמפים ברחבי אוסטרליה","short_summary":"A traveller documents a rare long-distance hitchhiking journey across Australia, exploring the history, legal challenges, and human connections of the practice.","english_level":"C1","words":461,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/travel/ng-interactive/2026/oct/10/hitchhiker-sydney-perth-company-of-strangers-free-travel","title":"I hitchhiked from Sydney to Perth, and found comfort in the company of strangers","published_at":"2026-10-09T14:00:33.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-09T14:00:33.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-10T12:51:47.585Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The practice of hitchhiking across Australia has long been a fading subculture, yet adventurous travellers still attempt ambitious cross-country routes. Recently, one traveller documented a remarkable journey from Sydney to Perth relying entirely on the kindness of motorists. While the trip offers a unique way to satisfy wanderlust at zero financial cost, it highlights the complex legal and historical realities surrounding the custom. Today, finding a hitchhiker on the side of Australian roads is quite rare.","Historically, hitchhiking enjoyed widespread popularity during the 1970s and 1980s. However, its reputation suffered severe damage in the early 1990s due to its association with serial killer Ivan Milat, who was convicted of murdering five female and two male backpackers in New South Wales between 1989 and 1992, with allegations of many more unsolved crimes. Furthermore, Australia remains one of the few nations where hitchhiking faces specific legal hurdles. According to reference resources like Hitchwiki, most regional jurisdictions prohibit pedestrians from standing on active roadways to solicit rides, although specific regulations differ between states and territories. For instance, Tasmania removed references to hitchhiking from its road rules in 2019, while the Australian Capital Territory permits it in most circumstances.","Despite safety concerns and legislative restrictions, there are indications that hitchhiking is experiencing a modest revival. Online communities such as Trustroots, which boasts more than 120,000 members, and Hitchwiki continue to expand. Meanwhile, social media influencers frequently share extreme travel content that demystifies the experience for a younger generation. Experts like Dr Fang Liu from the University of Western Australia note that while digital platforms inspire international travellers, newcomers often underestimate practical dangers such as dehydration during long waits in areas lacking mobile phone reception.","Throughout the recent transcontinental trip, the traveller experienced numerous generous encounters with diverse motorists. Rides included Doug Hilton, the head of Australia's national science agency CSIRO; a former Zimbabwean immigrant family who moved to Chinchilla after fleeing gun violence and immigration crackdowns in the US, finding a safe and welcoming community; a 67-year-old retiree named Mike who spends his time restoring century-old farm tractors; and a 79-year-old widower named Neil completing a four-month road trip. These varied conversations reflected broader social sentiments, from economic frustrations and job losses at industrial plants like the Whyalla steelworks to a deep appreciation for the country's vast open spaces.","Safety remains an inherent consideration for anyone attempting to secure rides along remote highways. Experienced practitioners generally adhere to specific safety guidelines, such as selecting locations with high visibility, maintaining sufficient room for vehicles to stop safely, and trusting one's instincts before entering any vehicle. While systemic risks vary depending on individual demographics—noting that women often face different dangers while hitching alone—the ongoing resurgence demonstrates that the willingness of strangers to offer assistance endures across the open road."],"facts":[{"fact":"Aston Brown undertook a hitchhiking journey across Australia from Sydney to Perth.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Hitchhiking declined in Australia following the 1990s murders committed by serial killer Ivan Milat.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Australian laws regarding hitchhiking vary by state and territory, with some jurisdictions explicitly prohibiting pedestrians from standing on roads to request rides.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Online platforms like Hitchwiki and Trustroots, alongside social media influencers, are helping normalise and revive interest in hitchhiking among young travellers.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"During his journey, Brown caught rides with various drivers, including Doug Hilton, a family from Zimbabwe, a retiree named Mike, and a 79-year-old widower named Neil.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"practice","lemma":"practice","pos":"noun","he":"תרגול / מנהג","name":false},{"text":"hitchhiking","lemma":"hitchhiking","pos":"noun","he":"טרמפיסטים","name":false},{"text":"across","lemma":"across","pos":"preposition","he":"ברחבי","name":false},{"text":"Australia","lemma":"Australia","pos":"proper noun","he":"אוסטרליה","name":true},{"text":"long","lemma":"long","pos":"adverb","he":"במשך זמן רב","name":false},{"text":"fading","lemma":"fade","pos":"adjective","he":"דועך","name":false},{"text":"subculture","lemma":"subculture","pos":"noun","he":"תת-תרבות","name":false},{"text":"yet","lemma":"yet","pos":"conjunction","he":"אף על פי כן","name":false},{"text":"adventurous","lemma":"adventurous","pos":"adjective","he":"הרפתקני","name":false},{"text":"travellers","lemma":"traveller","pos":"noun","he":"מטיילים","name":false},{"text":"still","lemma":"still","pos":"adverb","he":"עדיין","name":false},{"text